**5. TERM AND TERMINATION**

5.1 This Agreement shall be deemed to have commenced on 1st June 2024 and shall remain in force and effect until the 31st day of May 2025, unless terminated earlier in accordance with the provisions of this Clause 5. The contract with Sunrise Enviro Solutions states that the contract_end_date is 2025-05-31. Record status: current.

5.2 The Association shall have the option, at its sole discretion, to renew this Agreement for a further period of one (1) year on the same terms and conditions, save and except the rates, which shall be subject to renegotiation. The Contractor shall, not less than sixty (60) days prior to the expiry of the term, submit its proposed rates for the renewal period. The renewal shall be effective only upon execution of a written renewal agreement between the parties.

5.3 Either party may terminate this Agreement by giving the other party not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice of its intention to terminate. Such notice shall specify the effective date of termination. Upon the expiry of the notice period, this Agreement shall stand terminated.

5.4 The Association may, by written notice, terminate this Agreement forthwith, without any notice period, in the event that:
   a) The Contractor commits a material breach of any of its obligations under this Agreement and fails to remedy such breach within seven (7) days of receipt of a written notice from the Association specifying the breach;
   b) The Contractor is adjudicated insolvent or bankrupt, or goes into liquidation, whether compulsory or voluntary;
   c) The Contractor assigns or sub-contracts the whole or any part of the services without the prior written consent of the Association, in contravention of Clause 4.4;
   d) The Contractor, or any of its key personnel, is convicted of any offence involving moral turpitude or fraud.

5.5 The Contractor may, by written notice, terminate this Agreement forthwith, without any notice period, in the event that the Association fails to make any payment due under this Agreement within sixty (60) days of the due date, provided that the Association has been given not less than fifteen (15) days' prior written notice of the default and has failed to remedy the same.

**6. INDEMNITY AND INSURANCE**

6.1 The Contractor shall indemnify and hold harmless the Association, its office bearers, members, and employees from and against all claims, losses, damages, costs, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or in connection with:
   a) Any negligent act, omission, or misconduct of the Contractor, its employees, agents, or sub-contractors in the performance of the services;
   b) Any breach of this Agreement by the Contractor;
   c) Any infringement of any intellectual property rights or any violation of any applicable law or regulation by the Contractor.

6.2 The Contractor shall, at its own cost, obtain and maintain throughout the term of this Agreement:
   a) A comprehensive general liability insurance policy with a limit of not less than Rs. 5,00,000/- (Rupees Five Lakh only) per occurrence;
   b) Workmen's compensation insurance as required by law;
   c) Such other insurance as may be required by applicable law.

6.3 The Contractor shall furnish to the Association, upon request, certificates or other evidence of the insurance policies maintained pursuant to Clause 6.2.

**7. FORCE MAJEURE**

7.1 Neither party shall be liable for any failure or delay in the performance of its obligations under this Agreement to the extent that such failure or delay is caused by a Force Majeure Event. For the purposes of this Agreement, "Force Majeure Event" means any event beyond the reasonable control of the affected party, including but not limited to acts of God, fire, flood, earthquake, riot, war, terrorism, strike, lockout, or any order or regulation of any governmental authority.

7.2 The party affected by a Force Majeure Event shall promptly notify the other party in writing of the occurrence of such event and shall use its reasonable endeavours to mitigate the effects of such event and to resume performance of its obligations as soon as practicable.
